  "question": {
    "text": "A survey shows that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>63</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the people in a city read newspaper <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> whereas&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>76</mn><mo>%</mo></math> read news paper <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>. If&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;of the people read both the newspapers, then a possible value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> can be:"
